64913095?s=46&amp;t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/konstiwohlwend/status/2114848424264913095?s=46&amp;t=fSypFxt84bBHId-do9r5Ag</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:33:54 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[one (overstated) Chinese interpretation]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/profile_images/2028337523773038592/1kSOtKBU_400x400.jpg"></p><p>Phoenix Yin (@Phoenixyin13) on X</p><p>接下来就看一件事，PNP。 如果不远的未来AI已经逆天到可以成功证明 P=NP，而且算法真的实用，由于大部分加密都依赖验证容易破解很难，P=NP 意味着破解也能变容易。银行、HTTPS、加密货币，这些玩意全部得推倒重来。 而且优化问题会被打通。 现在困扰的排班、物流路线、芯片设计、蛋白质折叠这类问题，都能速速直接算出最优解。
数学研究本身被自动化，陶哲轩所说的数学工业时代必然进入高潮。因为检查一个证明是容易的，P=NP 意味着找到证明也会变得高效。很多猜想能让机器直接搜出证明。想想吧，冯诺伊曼也顶不住啊。 今天，我真的沉痛地思考了很久。人类一直默认欣赏一首好曲子比写出它容易，看懂一个证…</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/Phoenixyin13/status/2114949615493480863">https://x.com/Phoenixyin13/status/2114949615493480863</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/tuesday-assorted-links-592.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-592">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://x.com/Phoenixyin13/status/2114949615493480863</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://x.com/Phoenixyin13/status/2114949615493480863</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:33:54 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[another extreme and unwarranted view]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p>URL: <a href="https://emanueleviola.wordpress.com/2018/02/16/i-believe-pnp/">https://emanueleviola.wordpress.com/2018/02/16/i-believe-pnp/</a></p><p>source: <a href="https://marginalrevolution.com/marginalrevolution/2026/10/tuesday-assorted-links-592.html?utm_source=rss&utm_medium=rss&utm_campaign=tuesday-assorted-links-592">Tuesday assorted links</a></p>]]></description><link>https://emanueleviola.wordpress.com/2018/02/16/i-believe-pnp/</link><guid isPermaLink="true">https://emanueleviola.wordpress.com/2018/02/16/i-believe-pnp/</guid><pubDate>Tue, 27 Oct 2026 16:33:54 GMT</pubDate></item><item><title><![CDATA[New research method: Arjo Klamer’s revenge]]></title><description><![CDATA[<p><img src="https://pbs.twimg.com/media/HVi89TnWwAAx5Qg?format=webp&name=large"></p><p>The Review of Economic Studies (@RevEconStudies) on X</p><p>Can AI conduct qualitative interviews with thousands of people? In a new REStud paper, Friedrich Geiecke and @XJaravel develop an open-source approach that combines the depth of qualitative interviews with the scale of surveys. 1/6</p><p>URL: <a href="https://x.com/RevEconStudies/status/2114649281701261360">https://x.com/RevEconStudies/status/2114649281701261